# ctxloom's private working state: rebuildable or purely local, and so must
# never ride a distributable tree. Everything else here — config.yaml,
# remotes.yaml, lock.yaml, allowed_signers, approvals/, content/ — is committed
# by omission, because it is content, config, or trust state the project
# depends on.
#
# These patterns are gitignore.PrivateStatePatterns, relativized. This file is
# ctxloom's to own and rewrite; keep it in sync with that list rather than
# editing it by hand.
/cache
/sessions
/project-id
/state
# Advisory lock sidecars live under state/locks now, but a project written by an
# earlier version carries config.yaml.lock at this level, and leaving that
# visible in `git status` invites exactly one mistake.
*.lock
